From bf7cf5e8c0750ed8589039f336596bd539987d3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Greensi7 <adam.tabak04@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:38:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] crypto/asn1/asn1_lib.c: fix memory leak in
 ossl_asn1_string_set_internal()

A zero length ASN1_STRING can own a one byte buffer containing NUL byte.
When it is set again, passing NULL to OPENSSL_realloc() leaks that buffer.

Fixes: 28179061bfcd "Prepare a now opaque ASN1_STRING for the size_t rapture."
Original-Commit: 0dfd4cbc6d11 "crypto/asn1/asn1_lib.c: fix memory leak in ossl_asn1_string_set_internal()"
Original-PR: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33210
Reviewed-by: Milan Broz <mbroz@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Nikola Pajkovsky <nikolap@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Thu Nov 12 09:39:10 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33589
---
 crypto/asn1/asn1_lib.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crypto/asn1/asn1_lib.c b/crypto/asn1/asn1_lib.c
index a216525..dfd48b6 100644
--- a/crypto/asn1/asn1_lib.c
+++ b/crypto/asn1/asn1_lib.c
@@ -433,7 +433,7 @@ int ossl_asn1_string_set_internal(ASN1_STRING *str, const uint8_t *data,
 
     if ((size_t)str->length != alloc_len) {
         uint8_t *c;
-        c = OPENSSL_realloc(str->length == 0 ? NULL : str->data, alloc_len);
+        c = OPENSSL_realloc(str->data, alloc_len);
         if (c == NULL)
             return 0;
         str->data = c;
